  "full_text": "So you know there's perfect justice, right? So it begs the question, chicken or egg, when it comes to president and the American people, or king. Maybe you get the king you deserve or you don't deserve, or you get the president you don't deserve or you deserve. You know, when it comes to, maybe you have to change the country to get a better president or get a king. Like, who can change the country? Well... Somebody like Elvis could probably change the country. Somebody like the priest and stuff. So I'm totally, I'm flat broke. I'm 100 bucks in the hole, actually. And I'm sitting out here and basically, yeah, so I'm pretty much, yeah, I'm going to be eating the homeless food. But hey, look, I got God. You know, I run out of batteries. I can't broadcast anymore. So basically, I'm going to sit on Moses Mountain and you can fuck yourself. Because you get what you deserve, right? So fuck it. I got God, man. I'm cool, man. The Davis war cry is... Basically, what is it? Without... Let's see. Without anything, God is enough. Something like that. Anyway, go look it up on the Davis family. Look up Davis family war cry or something. And it says... Without anything, God, God is enough or something. Anyway, so, And when he had said these things, all his adversaries were ashamed, and all the people rejoiced for all the glorious things that were done by him. Then said he, Unto what is the kingdom of God like, and whereunto shall it resemble it? It was like a grain of mustard seed, which a man took, cast in the garden, grew, waxed, and followed the advice of the brethren. Waxed. He waxed.",
